/RC (<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><body style="font-family:ArialMT;font-size:5.5pt;color:#000000;text-align:left;line-height:7.3pt" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:9.0.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/"><p><span style="font-family:ArialMT;font-size:5.5pt;color:#000000;text-align:left;line-height:7.3pt">Co-treatment with CYP3A inhibitors, including cobicistat-containing products, is </span></p><p><span style="font-family:ArialMT;font-size:5.5pt;color:#000000;text-align:left;line-height:6.6pt">expected to &amp;#13;increase the risk of systemic side-effects. The combination should be avoided unless the &amp;#13;benefit outweights the increased risk of systemic corticosteroid side-effects, in which case &amp;#13;patients should be monitored for systemic costicosteroid side-effects.</span></p></body>)
